Havard,

I posted the same question on SE website <http://stackoverflow.com/questions/21534751/in-r-and-knitr-how-do-i-plot-inla-results>. Yihui Xie (developer of knitr package) suggested in the comments that:

I recommend you to contact the package author to remove the function inla.dev.new <http://inla.dev.new>. I do not think it makes sense: when in or not in RStudio, R will always automatically open a new device if a new plot comes -- there is no need to call dev.new <http://dev.new>() manually as the author did.

I'm still trying to get some better integration of INLA results with knitr using your exemplary code but still cannot use the full functionality of the package.

